{# MAN's tables.troubleshooting() macro for print (phase1-pdf-build.md §8,
   decision R-04): section 8.2 of chapter 8, one entry per symptom condition
   and one row per (condition, cause) pair.

   Both variants print the same cells, and the difference is the one spec §4
   asks for:

   * clean (`tables: fit_page`) gives every condition its own ## heading
     (id="cond-<id>", the number MAN's outline reserved) and its own table, so
     a table never breaks across a page;
   * realistic (`tables: span_pages_repeat_header`) prints one table that runs
     over page breaks with a single <thead> the stylesheet repeats, and starts
     each condition with a group row that carries the heading's id so every
     ref('cond:<id>') and the table of contents still land on a real element.

   A cause is two <tr>s (three for its full entry), because MAN's registry
   ids are up to 35 characters long and a 35-character id is 55 mm of IBM
   Plex Mono. Three narrow id columns beside three prose columns cost
   chapter 8 84 of the manual's 140 pages, and narrowing them broke every id
   over two lines, which destroys it in the extracted text (acceptance check
   #3 wants all 39 fault ids verbatim) — pdfplumber reads a page line by
   line, so the halves come back with other columns' words between them. So
   the ids get a band row of their own, where they have half the text block
   each and never wrap:

     <tr class="cause">   the identification band: condition id | fault id
                          (spanning two columns) | subsystem. This is the row
                          that carries id="fault-<id>", the data attributes
                          and, for check #4, the (condition_id, fault_id)
                          pair in its first two cells.
     <tr class="detail">  the four prose columns: possible cause, what to
                          check, remedy, see also.
     <tr class="signals"> the full entry only: one cell across the table,
                          "Signals:" and MAN's move_text() sentences, which
                          say which readings move, in which direction and in
                          which machine state (spec §3, "each cause states in
                          plain words which signals move"; chapter 8.1 sends
                          the reader to them). Run on after the summary in
                          the 27 % cause column, the sentences cost the clean
                          variant six pages and pushed it past the 50 of
                          spec §4; across the whole text block they cost two.

   Decision R-09 is kept — the fault id is a cell of its own on every cause
   row and the subsystem has one too — and the four prose columns now have
   173 mm between them instead of 133 mm, so the same text takes a quarter
   fewer lines. The <thead> names both rows, so a page that starts mid-table
   still says what each cell is.

   faults.yaml also shares 39 causes over 81 (condition, cause) pairs, so a
   row that always printed the whole entry printed the summary, the checks
   and the remedy 2.1 times each. The first condition that lists a cause —
   the one that already owns id="fault-<id>" and the section number
   ref('fault:<id>') resolves to — prints the entry in full; every later
   condition prints the cause name, the likelihood and its own note, and
   sends the reader to that section for the checks and the remedy, where the
   signals row is too. Both kinds of entry keep the band row and the
   (condition, fault) pair, so check #4 still recovers 81 rows. #}
{%- set columns = 4 -%}

{#- The section number the full entry of `fault_id` is printed under. -#}
{%- macro entry_ref(fault_id, owner_id) -%}
<a class="xref" href="#fault-{{ fault_id | e }}">{{ 'section ' if variant.xref_style == 'explicit' }}{{ sections['cond:' ~ owner_id].number | e }}</a>
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- The id of the first condition that lists `fault_id` (phase1-manual-content.md §8.3). -#}
{%- macro first_condition_id(fault_id) -%}
{%- set owner = namespace(id='') -%}
{%- for condition in manual.conditions -%}
{%- if not owner.id and (condition.causes | selectattr('fault_id', 'equalto', fault_id) | first is defined) -%}
{%- set owner.id = condition.id -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{{- owner.id -}}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro alarm_link(code) -%}
<a class="xref" href="#alarm-{{ code | e }}"><span class="alarm-code">{{ code | e }}</span></a>
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- Maintenance tasks and controller messages to follow up from one cause. -#}
{%- macro see_also(cause) -%}
{%- set codes = namespace(list=[]) -%}
{%- for condition in manual.conditions -%}
{%- if condition.causes | selectattr('fault_id', 'equalto', cause.fault_id) | first is defined -%}
{%- for code in condition.alarms -%}
{%- if code not in codes.list -%}{%- set codes.list = codes.list + [code] -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if not cause.maintenance and not codes.list -%}&mdash;
{%- else -%}
{%- for task_id in cause.maintenance -%}
<a class="xref" href="#task-{{ task_id | e }}">{{ manual.task(task_id).name | e }}</a>{{ ', ' if not loop.last }}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if cause.maintenance and codes.list %}; {% endif -%}
{%- for code in codes.list %}{{ alarm_link(code) }}{{ ', ' if not loop.last }}{% endfor -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro cause_row(condition, entry) -%}
{%- set cause = manual.cause(entry.fault_id) -%}
{%- set owner_id = first_condition_id(cause.fault_id) | trim -%}
{%- set owns = owner_id == condition.id -%}
<tr class="cause{{ '' if owns else ' repeat' }}"{% if owns %} id="fault-{{ cause.fault_id | e }}"{% endif %} data-condition="{{ condition.id | e }}" data-fault="{{ cause.fault_id | e }}" data-likelihood="{{ entry.likelihood | e }}">
<td class="condition-id"><span class="mono">{{ condition.id | e }}</span></td>
<td class="fault-id" colspan="2"><span class="mono">{{ cause.fault_id | e }}</span></td>
<td class="subsystem">{{ cause.subsystem | replace('_', ' ') | e }}</td>
</tr>
<tr class="detail{{ '' if owns else ' repeat' }}" data-condition="{{ condition.id | e }}" data-fault="{{ cause.fault_id | e }}">
{%- if owns %}
<td><span class="cause-name">{{ cause.name | e }}</span> ({{ entry.likelihood | e }}{{ ', benign' if cause.benign }})<br>{{ cause.summary_html }}
{%- if entry.note_html %} {{ entry.note_html }}{% endif %}</td>
<td><ul class="checks">
{%- for check in cause.checks_html %}<li>{{ check }}</li>{% endfor -%}
</ul></td>
<td>{{ cause.remedy_html }}</td>
{%- else %}
<td><span class="cause-name">{{ cause.name | e }}</span> ({{ entry.likelihood | e }}{{ ', benign' if cause.benign }})
{%- if entry.note_html %}<br>{{ entry.note_html }}{% endif %}</td>
<td>The checks of {{ entry_ref(cause.fault_id, owner_id) }}.</td>
<td>The remedy of {{ entry_ref(cause.fault_id, owner_id) }}.</td>
{%- endif %}
<td>{{ see_also(cause) }}</td>
</tr>
{%- if owns %}
<tr class="signals" data-condition="{{ condition.id | e }}" data-fault="{{ cause.fault_id | e }}"><td colspan="{{ columns }}"><span class="signals-label">Signals:</span> {{ man.move_text(cause.fault_id) | join(' ') | e }}</td></tr>
{%- endif %}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- Fixed column widths: see the `.troubleshooting col` rules of base.css. -#}
{%- macro colgroup() -%}
<colgroup><col class="c-cause"><col class="c-checks"><col class="c-remedy"><col class="c-see-also"></colgroup>
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro header_row() -%}
<tr class="band-head"><th>Condition</th><th colspan="2">Fault id</th><th>Subsystem</th></tr>
<tr><th>Possible cause</th><th>What to check</th><th>Remedy</th><th>See also</th></tr>
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro condition_intro(condition) -%}
<p class="symptom">{{ condition.symptom_html }}</p>
{% if condition.alarms %}
<p class="typical-messages">Typical messages:
{% for code in condition.alarms %}{{ alarm_link(code) }}{{ ', ' if not loop.last else '.' }}{% endfor %}</p>
{% endif %}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro per_condition() -%}
{% for condition in manual.conditions %}
{%- set section = sections['cond:' ~ condition.id] -%}
<h2 id="{{ section.html_id | e }}"><span class="num">{{ section.number | e }}</span> {{ section.title | e }} <span class="mono condition-id">{{ condition.id | e }}</span></h2>
{{ condition_intro(condition) }}
<table class="troubleshooting" data-condition="{{ condition.id | e }}">
{{ colgroup() }}
<thead>{{ header_row() }}</thead>
<tbody>
{% for entry in condition.causes %}{{ cause_row(condition, entry) }}
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
{% endfor %}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro spanning() -%}
<table class="troubleshooting spanning">
<caption>Symptoms, causes and remedies</caption>
{{ colgroup() }}
<thead>{{ header_row() }}</thead>
<tbody>
{% for condition in manual.conditions %}
{%- set section = sections['cond:' ~ condition.id] -%}
<tr class="group" id="{{ section.html_id | e }}"><td colspan="{{ columns }}"><span class="num">{{ section.number | e }}</span> {{ section.title | e }} <span class="mono condition-id">{{ condition.id | e }}</span><span class="symptom"> &mdash; {{ condition.symptom_html }}</span></td></tr>
{% for entry in condition.causes %}{{ cause_row(condition, entry) }}
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro troubleshooting() -%}
{%- if variant.tables == 'span_pages_repeat_header' -%}
{{ spanning() }}
{%- else -%}
{{ per_condition() }}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}
